The bug occurs because Ceph's directory operations in `ceph_finish_lookup()` and `ceph_lookup()` incorrectly assume that any negative dentry passed to `d_add(dentry, NULL)` is always unhashed. In reality, cached negative dentries can already be present in the dcache hash table. Calling `d_add()` on an already-hashed dentry causes `__d_rehash()` to reinsert the same node, corrupting the hash bucket (e.g., creating a self-loop). This leads to infinite loops in `__d_lookup()` and eventual RCU stall panics.

